Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 03:03:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] docs(backend): say out loud why the second reuse read stays,
 and what measured it (ORD-0224 disposition 2)

Mutant Y1b at f92f9e9 switched `existing = find_open_operation(session, fingerprint)` off and all
twelve doors stayed green, so no gate depends on this read today - it is a second chance behind the
pre-resolution read and in front of the durable index + loser read-back that carry convergence (Y3).
Kept by the commander's order; behaviour and the anchor for future mutations are unchanged (the
anchor still counts exactly 1), so only a comment moved.

Readings after the edit (same interpreter, `-X utf8`): gates + weak-fix doors + measurement package
= 19 collected, 18 passed / 1 failed (`test_g5_an_ai_run_that_changed_must_say_which_it_was`,
pre-existing and owned by ORD-0218).
---
 backend/app/catalog_hydration_operations.py | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/backend/app/catalog_hydration_operations.py b/backend/app/catalog_hydration_operations.py
index bc2ba60..c6fe73e 100644
--- a/backend/app/catalog_hydration_operations.py
+++ b/backend/app/catalog_hydration_operations.py
@@ -467,6 +467,12 @@ def submit_operation(
         resolution.canonical_destination_id,
         resolver_query_normalized=resolution.resolver_query_normalized,
     )
+    # Kept by the commander's disposition (ORD-0224, 2026-09-23 03:0x) and by measurement, not by
+    # habit: mutant **Y1b** at `f92f9e9` switched this read off and all twelve doors stayed green, so
+    # **no gate depends on it today** - it is a second chance, behind the pre-resolution read and in
+    # front of the durable index + loser read-back that actually carry convergence (`Y3`).  Deleting it
+    # now would reopen the concurrency path for no evidence, and that is the strong fix's work surface;
+    # if it ever goes, it goes in that order, in writing.
     existing = find_open_operation(session, fingerprint)
     if existing is not None:
         return existing, True
